Fenris was once the Titan of [[Thor]] himself and was left to guard the restricted caves beneath the [[Temple of Thor]] long after his Seeker's death. With the magic of Thor's temple keeping Fenris invoked through the centuries, he remained active and rabid for thousands of years into the modern age. {{Source|Two Powers Become One}}

While both the [[Huntik Foundation]] and [[the Organization]] were trying to find [[Mjolnir]], the Hammer of Thor, the wild Titan, Fenris, was also discovered past the Door of Infinity. Virtually invulnerable to attacks due to the magic of the temple, Fenris attempted to attack [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] team, but he eventually tied up with the [[Rope of Gleipnir]] using some help from [[Springer]]. As the magical rope could not be broken, Fenris was constricted and eventually send back to his [[Amulet]]. Dante picked up the Amulet and gave it to [[Montehue]] after the mission, believing Fenris would bond readily to a Seeker with a character close to that of Thor. {{source|Two Powers Become One}}

During the mission to acquire the [[Ring]] of [[Tao]], Montehue summoned Fenris to fight the three colossi outside [[King Solomon's mines]]. Fenris teamed up with Lok's [[Lindorm]] to defeat [[Ashtoreth]]. Later, in the mines, Fenris battled against [[Dominator]]. When Dominator's spikes became lodged in Fenris, his ability caused Fenris to temporarily revert to his berserk state and refuse to listen to Montehue. {{source|To Be Together}}

Fenris was later used by Montehue in [[Indonesia]] to fight against a [[Silent Soldiers|Silent Soldier's]] [[Shadow Kuolit]]. Fenris proved to be faster than the Shadow Kuolit, who attempted to slice him, but the shadows from Shadow Kuolit's body injured the wolf Titan. {{source|The Dead Magic Island}}  The following day, Fenris helped Montehue fight numerous [[Blood Spiral]] forces and later witnessed [[Sophie Casterwill]] rising from the lava of a volcano with [[Phoenix]], the Legendary Titan of Rebirth. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

Fenris fought in the battle at the [[Blood Spiral Base]]. He saved [[Scarlet Byrne]] from a [[Nighlurker]] Titan before being floored himself by a [[Marauder]]. He was then saved when the Marauder was picked up and defeated by Scarlet's [[Firbolg]] Titan. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}}
